Design a circuit that implements Manchester encoding and decoding. The module takes a single bit of input data and produces a Manchester encoded output, which is a signal that represents both the data and a clock signal, ensuring synchronization. The output `data_out` reflects the decoded value based on the transitions of the incoming data, while `clock_out` provides a regular clock signal that is an inverted version of the previous state. This design effectively converts binary information into a format suitable for transmission over noisy channels while also generating a reliable clock reference signal.
