description:
Design a circuit that functions as a signal level slicer. It takes a signed 18-bit input signal and a reference level, producing a 2-bit output based on the comparison between the input signal and the reference. The output indicates whether the input is above a specific threshold, within a defined positive range, within a defined negative range, or below both, thereby categorizing the input signal into four distinct states. This module operates on the rising edge of a clock signal, ensuring synchronized output changes.
module top_module(
	input clk,
    input signed [17:0] slicer_in, ref_level,
    output reg [1:0] slicer_out
);

code:
module top_module(
	input clk,
    input signed [17:0] slicer_in, ref_level,
    output reg [1:0] slicer_out
);always @ (posedge clk)
    if (slicer_in >= ref_level)	
        slicer_out <= 2'b11;
    else if (slicer_in > 18'sd0)	
        slicer_out <= 2'b10;
    else if (slicer_in > -ref_level)	
        slicer_out <= 2'b01;
    else
        slicer_out <= 2'b00;	

endmodule

