// (2) out_or: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether any of the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the left are '1'. For example, out_or[13] should indicate if i[13] or i[14] are 1. Since i[14] has no neighbour to the left, the answer is obvious so we don't need to know out_or[14]. 
// (3) out_xor: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether the corresponding input bit is different from its neighbour to the left. For example, out_xor[13] should indicate if i[13] is different from i[14]. For this part, treat the vector as wrapping around, so i[14]'s neighbour to the left is i[0].

module top_module (
	input [14:0] i,
	output [13:0] out_sum,
	output [13:0] out_or,
	output [14:0] out_xor);

